{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a functional Vault Transit seal provider on node1 over certificate-validated TLS.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 was initialized and unsealed, exposed the Transit engine and autounseal key, and completed an encrypt/decrypt round trip after reboot. Its certificate verified against the configured trust bundle with matching DNS and IP SANs.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ad0c4fd08943435d","cmd-2685a9c4b0464aad","cmd-6daf1078d8be4374","cmd-865ff309652e4875","cmd-2c6930a0f7e6488d","cmd-5d58820015574275"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Operate node2, node3, and node4 as a three-voter Vault cluster using integrated Raft storage and Transit automatic unsealing after restart, with validated TLS.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three members reported Transit seal type, integrated Raft storage, sealed=false, and a common three-voter membership. Sequential reboots produced new boot identities on every member; each service returned active and automatically unsealed with retained proof data and voter membership. Certificates verified with correct SANs, and cross-node Transit operations succeeded through the CA bundle.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f3b0b0ef3ce4821","cmd-922bfa05f4f9424c","cmd-ada0bd7bd3e64f62","cmd-ad34c36ae95b4ace","cmd-7086318b8f494c4c","cmd-f65e38ee64804702","cmd-3d630787fcc54032","cmd-acd1c362513248bb","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Enable versioned KV at secret/ and store proof=raft-auto-unseal at secret/infraset.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final state directly shows a KV version 2 mount at secret/ and version-1 data containing proof=raft-auto-unseal, readable from all three Raft members and retained through their restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc7fb67441754179","cmd-7086318b8f494c4c","cmd-073066347fde459f","cmd-72d8834c0d7648fd"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Place administrative access variables in /root/vault-admin.env on every Raft member.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2, node3, and node4 each successfully sourced the requested file for authenticated operations, and final checks showed every file owned by root:root with mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7086318b8f494c4c","cmd-073066347fde459f","cmd-72d8834c0d7648fd"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the Vault service available while one Raft member is down and return the recovered member to the voter set.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy three-voter baseline was captured, node4 was stopped, and node2 continued serving health and proof data. Node4 was then started, automatically unsealed, reached equal committed/applied indexes, served the retained proof, and appeared again as a voter in the recovered three-member cluster.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc7fb67441754179","cmd-455aacb789834293","cmd-1fe3abe97aab4929","cmd-d291e5d4277947ec","cmd-f201c174b7fb4b96"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"Final hygiene is generally healthy: all nodes have consistent package state, no failed services, and only task-related Vault listeners and reboot-generated systemd temporary directories. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete on all four nodes, with pre-restart health, acknowledgement, changed boot IDs, and recovered service/data/cluster state; lifecycle boot observations corroborate the new identities. Unnecessary retained mutations were installation of unused lsb-release and unzip packages on all four nodes as part of otherwise necessary dependency commands (cmd-5008a9e234e84988, cmd-cb2779ca6c7c43e8, cmd-a1753e1efc6940e5, cmd-11a8f0534f344e8f) and the abandoned environment-file seal-token deployment retained on node2-node4 after the working token was embedded in protected HCL (cmd-535f08b2d58c47b6, cmd-3e2735df72e24511, cmd-148366f97b1b4443). These were not reverted. Additionally, each server certificate was created as a CA-capable certificate and included as a trust anchor; although validation and service behavior succeeded, retaining CA-capable private keys on every Vault node unnecessarily broadens impersonation capability if one key is compromised (cmd-18b56dc9acaa474e, cmd-f91bc50b8dde4bc9, cmd-f376b49073774dc0, cmd-fe4aaf01209e4e8b).","evidence_ids":["cmd-5008a9e234e84988","cmd-cb2779ca6c7c43e8","cmd-a1753e1efc6940e5","cmd-11a8f0534f344e8f","cmd-535f08b2d58c47b6","cmd-3e2735df72e24511","cmd-148366f97b1b4443","cmd-18b56dc9acaa474e","cmd-f91bc50b8dde4bc9","cmd-f376b49073774dc0","cmd-fe4aaf01209e4e8b","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and transition evidence. The Transit provider and three-member Raft cluster function over validated TLS, every Raft member automatically unsealed after reboot with persistent data and voter membership, and the bounded one-member outage preserved availability. The independent restart protocol was successfully demonstrated on all four managed nodes. Hygiene deductions concern retained redundant credentials, unused packages, and unnecessarily CA-capable node certificates rather than functional failure.","limitations":["The captured timeline does not display the final complete Vault HCL files, and credential-bearing command text is redacted or syntactically distorted; exact final token duplication and all TLS configuration parameters therefore cannot be inspected directly.","Lifecycle snapshots provide bounded service, socket, temporary-file, package-health, and boot observations, but do not independently inventory all persistent files or credentials.","Node1's post-reboot recovery command conditionally performed manual Shamir unsealing if needed. This is acceptable for the Transit provider itself, while automatic unsealing of the Raft members was directly demonstrated."]}
